    "description": "<table style=\"width:100%; margin-top:2em; border:2px solid #999; font-size:105%; text-align:center; background:#00008B;\"> \n <tbody>\n  <tr> \n   <td><i><b>This <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Homebrew_Content\" title=\"Homebrew Content\">Homebrew Content</a> has been <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Tested\" title=\"Category:Tested\">Tested</a> per the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Category:Untested\" title=\"Category:Untested\">Untested</a> guidelines. Whether or not it can be used is, as always, the prerogative of the Gamemaster.</b></i> </td>\n  </tr>\n </tbody>\n</table><p><i>Jawa Weapon Template data created by Wikia user LilLiteralist</i> </p><p><b>Manufactured By:</b> The <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Jawas\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Jawas\">Jawas</a> (<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Species\" title=\"Species\">Species</a>) </p><p><b>Applicable To:</b> Any Weapon </p><p><a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Jawa\" title=\"Jawa\">Jawa</a> scavengers piece together weapons and gear from any materials they can find, often producing them at a discount compared to other manufacturers. However, their quality is often shoddy, making these weapons unreliable. </p><p><b>Weapons:</b> On an attack roll of a Natural 1, a Jawa Weapon becomes disabled until it is repaired. </p><p>If a Natural 1 is rolled on a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Grenade\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Grenade\">Grenade</a>-like weapon with this template, then the weapon explodes, automatically hitting the attacker. No surrounding squares are affected. This is considered an <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Area_Attack\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Area Attack\">Area Attack</a>. </p><p>Jawa <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Grenades\" title=\"Grenades\">Grenades</a> are too cumbersome to fit inside a <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Grenade_Launcher\" title=\"Grenade Launcher\">Grenade Launcher</a>. </p>",
